PracticeItems.Prompt:
Consider the following class:

public class Printer {
    public static void printLine(String text) {
        System.out.println("Line: " + text);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        printLine("Hello");
        System.out.println("Done");
    }
}

What is printed when main runs?

public class Greeter {
    public static void greet() {
        System.out.println("Hi there");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = greet();
        System.out.println(x);
    }
}

What happens when this code is compiled?

public class Counter {
    public static void showCount(int n) {
        System.out.println("Count is " + n);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 3;
        showCount(a);
        showCount(a + 2);
    }
}

How many times does control leave main to run showCount's frame, and what are the two lines printed?
